# This skill compares bytes, so line endings are part of its contract rather than a matter of
# taste. The evals diff generated output against a committed golden file, and verify.mjs
# byte-matches the runtime embedded in a document against dist/widget.min.js. A clone made with
# core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default — rewrites both to CRLF on checkout, and every one of
# those comparisons then fails on output that is perfectly correct. Diagnosing that costs an
# hour and ends in someone "fixing" a golden file. Pin the subtree instead.
* text eol=lf

# The exception is the fixture whose entire purpose is to BE a CRLF document: eval 11-crlf
# asserts that CRLF line endings outside the injected block survive injection untouched.
# Normalising it would delete the thing it tests.
test/fixtures/edge-crlf.html -text
